{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:70f51214079655c7", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Diversification", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "The idea is that if one investment loses money, other investments may make up for some of those losses.", "question": "What is diversification, and how might it help manage investment risk?", "answer": "Diversification means spreading investments across different kinds of assets rather than relying on just one. If one investment loses value, others may make up for some of the losses, though diversification does not guarantee against losses.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 158}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:70f51214079655c7", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Diversification", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Diversification can help reduce your losses if the market drops", "question": "Misconception: If I diversify my investments, I’m guaranteed not to lose money when the market drops.", "answer": "Diversification can help reduce losses, but it does not guarantee that you will avoid them. The source says other investments may make up for some losses, while noting that all investments involve risk.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 300}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:1d1ee2d66dedfc20", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Concentration Risk", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "You could buy shares of a single company, but then your financial performance will depend exclusively on how that single company’s stock performs.", "question": null, "answer": "Concentration risk is the risk of relying heavily on one investment or a narrow group of investments. For example, if you own shares in only one company, your financial performance depends on how that company’s stock performs. Diversifying across different kinds of assets can help reduce the impact of a loss in one investment, though it does not eliminate investment risk.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 238}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:1d1ee2d66dedfc20", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Concentration Risk", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "You could buy shares of a single company, but then your financial performance will depend exclusively on how that single company’s stock performs.", "question": "What is concentration risk in investing, and how can diversification help address it?", "answer": "Concentration risk is the risk of relying heavily on one investment, such as a single company’s stock, so your results depend on how that investment performs. Diversifying across different kinds of assets can help reduce losses if one investment falls, because others may make up for some of them. It does not guarantee that losses will be avoided.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 242}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:1d1ee2d66dedfc20", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Concentration Risk", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "You could buy shares of a single company, but then your financial performance will depend exclusively on how that single company’s stock performs.", "question": "Misconception: Investing in just one company does not create concentration risk as long as the company is well known.", "answer": "A well-known company’s stock can still lose value. If you invest in only one company, your financial performance depends exclusively on how that stock performs. Spreading investments among different kinds of assets can help reduce the impact if one investment loses money.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 317}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:4dace1648f0878b9", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Index Funds", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "An index fund is a product that seeks to track a market index, which measures the performance of a “basket” of stocks and bonds and is representative of a stock market or an economy.", "question": null, "answer": "An index fund is an investment product designed to track a market index. The index measures the performance of a basket of stocks and bonds that represents a stock market or an economy. In other words, rather than tracking just one company, an index fund seeks to follow the performance of that broader market measure. Like other investments, it involves risk.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 201}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:4dace1648f0878b9", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Index Funds", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "An index fund is a product that seeks to track a market index, which measures the performance of a “basket” of stocks and bonds and is representative of a stock market or an economy.", "question": "What is an index fund designed to do?", "answer": "An index fund seeks to track a market index. That index measures the performance of a basket of stocks and bonds representing a stock market or an economy.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 222}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:4dace1648f0878b9", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Index Funds", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "An index fund is a product that seeks to track a market index, which measures the performance of a “basket” of stocks and bonds and is representative of a stock market or an economy.", "question": "Misconception: An index fund represents just one company, so its performance depends entirely on that company’s stock.", "answer": "An index fund seeks to track a market index, which measures a basket of stocks and bonds representing a stock market or economy. It is therefore designed to provide exposure to a broader cross-section of the market rather than just one company.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 270}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:7b9456b72654ce94", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Workplace Retirement Accounts", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "A workplace retirement plan, like a 401(k) or a 403(b) or 457(b) is a benefit of many jobs. Contributing to one may reduce the amount of taxes you pay. Many employers match contributions you make up to a certain amount.", "question": null, "answer": "A workplace retirement account is a plan offered through many jobs to help employees save and invest for retirement. Examples include 401(k), 403(b), and 457(b) plans. Contributions may reduce the amount of taxes you pay, and some employers match contributions up to a limit. If your employer offers a match, contributing at least enough to receive the full match can help you take advantage of those matching funds. After contributing, you choose how to invest the money from the options in the plan.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 399}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:7b9456b72654ce94", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Workplace Retirement Accounts", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Many employers match contributions you make up to a certain amount.", "question": "What is one potential benefit of contributing to a workplace retirement plan?", "answer": "Some employers match employee contributions up to a certain amount. If your employer offers a match, contributing enough to receive it may let you take full advantage of those matching funds. Workplace plans may also provide tax advantages.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 157}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:7b9456b72654ce94", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Workplace Retirement Accounts", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Many employers match contributions you make up to a certain amount.", "question": "Misconception: If I contribute to a workplace retirement plan, my employer will match every dollar I contribute without limit.", "answer": "An employer match may be limited: many employers match contributions only up to a certain amount. Check your plan’s terms to learn its matching limit.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 212}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:bdd60f63a0ee5290", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Individual Retirement Accounts", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Another type of retirement saving account is one that you set up yourself, known as an Individual Retirement Account or IRA.", "question": null, "answer": "An Individual Retirement Account (IRA) is a retirement savings account you set up yourself. It lets you invest in your own tax-advantaged account to help provide financial security in retirement. IRA contributions can also reduce the amount you pay in taxes. You can have both an IRA and an employer-provided retirement plan, though annual contribution limits apply.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 170}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:bdd60f63a0ee5290", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Individual Retirement Accounts", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Another type of retirement saving account is one that you set up yourself, known as an Individual Retirement Account or IRA. You can invest in your own tax-advantaged investment account to provide financial security when you retire.", "question": "What is an Individual Retirement Account (IRA)?", "answer": "An IRA is a retirement savings account that you set up yourself. It is a tax-advantaged investment account intended to help provide financial security in retirement.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 162}}
