{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:c6c9d2d7deb16b9d", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Exchange-Traded Funds", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Once you contribute to a retirement-focused investment account, you will have options for how you want to invest the contribution you and your employer have made.", "question": "Misconception: Contributing to a workplace retirement plan means your contribution is automatically invested in an ETF.", "answer": "A contribution to a retirement account does not necessarily go into an ETF automatically. The source says you have options for how to invest your contributions, and notes that many people choose mutual funds or ETFs.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2887, "output_tokens": 411}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:b6d03571d0e87765", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Target Date Funds", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Target date funds in these accounts may automatically shift toward a more conservative mix of investments as you approach your anticipated retirement date.", "question": null, "answer": "A target date fund is an investment option that may adjust its investment mix over time. As you get closer to the retirement date you anticipate, it may shift toward a more conservative mix. This adjustment is not a guarantee against investment losses; all investments involve some risk.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 203}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:b6d03571d0e87765", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Target Date Funds", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Target date funds in these accounts may automatically shift toward a more conservative mix of investments as you approach your anticipated retirement date.", "question": "How may a target date fund change its investments as you get closer to your anticipated retirement date?", "answer": "It may automatically shift toward a more conservative mix of investments as your anticipated retirement date approaches.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 153}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:b6d03571d0e87765", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Target Date Funds", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "All investments have some degree of risk.\nTarget date funds in these accounts may automatically shift toward a more conservative mix of investments as you approach your anticipated retirement date.", "question": "Misconception: A target date fund guarantees a return and removes investment risk. Is that true?", "answer": "No. A target date fund may automatically shift toward a more conservative mix as you approach your anticipated retirement date, but investments still carry risk. The shift does not guarantee a return or eliminate the possibility of losses.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": false, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 413}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:410b07403434067b", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Short-Term Savings", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "A savings account is a good choice for short-term goals or to hold an emergency fund that can cover unexpected expenses.", "question": null, "answer": "For goals that are coming up soon, such as buying a car or making a near-term house down payment, think about how quickly you may need to use the money. A savings account can suit short-term goals or an emergency fund. The source also notes that short-term funds are generally kept somewhere they can be accessed quickly without tax penalties or significant fees. Some people seeking investments for these goals consider options with less potential risk and volatility, such as money market funds, CDs, or investment-grade bonds.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 254}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:410b07403434067b", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Short-Term Savings", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "A savings account is a good choice for short-term goals or to hold an emergency fund that can cover unexpected expenses.", "question": "What type of account does the source identify as a good option for short-term savings?", "answer": "The source identifies a savings account as a good choice for short-term goals or for holding an emergency fund for unexpected expenses.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 208}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:410b07403434067b", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Short-Term Savings", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "A savings account is a good choice for short-term goals or to hold an emergency fund that can cover unexpected expenses.", "question": "Misconception: A savings account is not suitable for short-term goals; short-term money should only be invested.", "answer": "A savings account can be a good choice for short-term goals or an emergency fund. The source also notes that some people seeking short-term investments may consider options with less potential risk and volatility, such as money market funds, CDs, or investment-grade bonds.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 211}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:4d46b6c8b3f55335", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Certificates of Deposit", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "you may be seeking investments with less potential risk and volatility such as money market funds, certificates of deposit (CDs) or investment grade bonds.", "question": null, "answer": "Certificates of deposit (CDs) are listed as one option to consider for short-term goals, such as buying a car or making a near-term down payment, when you are seeking investments with less potential risk and volatility. The source does not describe CD terms or guarantees, so check those details before deciding whether a CD fits your needs.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 259}}
