{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:ecd245ab44616584", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Budgeting", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Start by listing your income, expenses, savings and investment contributions. Prioritize long-term saving and investing goals by setting up automatic contributions to those, while making sure your income covers your monthly living expenses. Live within your means.", "question": null, "answer": "A budget helps you plan how to use your money. List your income, expenses, savings, and investment contributions. Prioritize long-term saving and investing goals, and consider setting up automatic contributions. Make sure your income covers your monthly living expenses and live within your means.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 205}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:ecd245ab44616584", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Budgeting", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Start by listing your income, expenses, savings and investment contributions.", "question": "When making a budget as an introductory investor, what should you list?", "answer": "List your income, expenses, savings, and investment contributions. You can prioritize long-term saving and investing goals with automatic contributions while ensuring your income covers monthly living expenses.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 152}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:ecd245ab44616584", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Budgeting", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Start by listing your income, expenses, savings and investment contributions.", "question": "Misconception: A budget only needs to track income and monthly spending; saving and investing do not belong in it.", "answer": "A budget can include savings and investment contributions as well as income and expenses. The source recommends prioritizing long-term saving and investing goals while making sure your income covers monthly living expenses.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 170}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d195f7b437c21c7d", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "High-Interest Debt", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "If you don’t pay off that balance every month, you’ll be paying interest charges that may greatly exceed the amount you could earn on your savings or investments.", "question": null, "answer": "High-interest credit card debt can work against your efforts to build wealth: if you carry a balance instead of paying it off each month, the interest charges may greatly exceed what you could earn on savings or investments. The source recommends considering aggressive steps to pay off high-interest debt and limiting credit card use.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2887, "output_tokens": 238}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d195f7b437c21c7d", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "High-Interest Debt", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "If you don’t pay off that balance every month, you’ll be paying interest charges that may greatly exceed the amount you could earn on your savings or investments.", "question": "Why might paying down high-interest credit card debt be an important step before focusing on growing savings or investments?", "answer": "If you carry a credit card balance, the interest charges may greatly exceed what you could earn on savings or investments. Paying down that debt can therefore be an important part of a wealth-building plan.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2887, "output_tokens": 192}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:d195f7b437c21c7d", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "High-Interest Debt", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "you’ll be paying interest charges that may greatly exceed the amount you could earn on your savings or investments.", "question": "Misconception: “I should always invest extra money before paying down high-interest credit card debt because investing can earn returns.”", "answer": "High-interest credit card debt can cost more in interest than savings or investments may earn. The source recommends considering aggressive repayment of that debt and limiting credit card use, especially if you do not pay the balance off each month.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2887, "output_tokens": 226}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:43547eaf8f7c6e22", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Emergency Funds", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "A savings account is a good choice for short-term goals or to hold an emergency fund that can cover unexpected expenses.", "question": null, "answer": "An emergency fund is money set aside for unexpected expenses, such as a car repair. Keeping these funds in a savings account can help you cover an unexpected cost without needing to go into debt.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 219}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:43547eaf8f7c6e22", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Emergency Funds", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Many investors use their bank or credit union to set aside some “rainy day” funds so that they don’t have to go into debt if they have an unexpected expense, like a car repair.", "question": "What is the purpose of an emergency fund?", "answer": "An emergency fund is money set aside for unexpected expenses, such as a car repair. It can help you avoid going into debt to cover those costs.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 156}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:43547eaf8f7c6e22", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Emergency Funds", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "A savings account is a good choice for short-term goals or to hold an emergency fund that can cover unexpected expenses.", "question": "Misconception: An emergency fund should be invested in stocks so it can grow over time. What is a better way to think about it?", "answer": "An emergency fund is meant to help cover unexpected expenses, so it is generally better suited to savings than to investments that can fluctuate in value. The source identifies a savings account as a good choice for holding an emergency fund.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2885, "output_tokens": 211}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:82c4fa4de86af042", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Investment Fraud Prevention", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Learning the tactics scammers use and how to spot the red flags of investment fraud will help you keep your money safe.", "question": null, "answer": "Investment fraud prevention begins with awareness: learn the tactics scammers use and watch for warning signs of fraud. Recognizing red flags can help you protect your money. The source recommends learning these tactics and signs but does not list specific examples.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 179}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:82c4fa4de86af042", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Investment Fraud Prevention", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Learning the tactics scammers use and how to spot the red flags of investment fraud will help you keep your money safe.", "question": "According to the source, what can investors do to help protect their investments from fraud?", "answer": "Learn the tactics scammers use and how to spot the red flags of investment fraud.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 194}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:82c4fa4de86af042", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Investment Fraud Prevention", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Scammers use a variety of techniques to convince investors to hand over their hard-earned money. Learning the tactics scammers use and how to spot the red flags of investment fraud will help you keep your money safe.", "question": "Misconception: If I understand that investments can lose value, I don’t need to learn about investment fraud. Is that correct?", "answer": "No. Market fluctuations and investment fraud are separate risks to consider. Scammers may use techniques to persuade investors to hand over money, so learning their tactics and recognizing fraud red flags can help protect your money.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 345}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:c716cf5d7d72f8e0", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Money Market Funds", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "In those situations, you may be seeking investments with less potential risk and volatility such as money market funds, certificates of deposit (CDs) or investment grade bonds.", "question": null, "answer": "Money market funds are one type of investment the source lists as a possible option for short-term goals, such as saving for a car or a near-term house down payment, when someone is seeking less potential risk and volatility. That does not mean they are risk-free: the source notes that all investments involve some degree of risk.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 278}}
