{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:misconception:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:c716cf5d7d72f8e0", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Money Market Funds", "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "All investments have some degree of risk. In those situations, you may be seeking investments with less potential risk and volatility such as money market funds, certificates of deposit (CDs) or investment grade bonds.", "question": "Misconception: Money market funds are risk-free because they can be used for short-term goals.", "answer": "Money market funds are listed as an option for short-term goals when someone is seeking investments with less potential risk and volatility. That does not mean they are risk-free: the source states that all investments have some degree of risk.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": false, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 664}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:tutorial:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:6e01e7e7be7d9894", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Asset Liquidity", "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Funds for short-term goals are generally held in an account that allows you to access the funds quickly without any tax penalties or significant fees.", "question": null, "answer": "Asset liquidity is about how quickly and easily you can access your money. For a goal coming up soon, the source suggests keeping funds in an account that allows quick access without significant fees or tax penalties. A savings account is also described as a good choice for short-term goals or emergencies.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 217}}
{"id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971:qa:gpt-6-luna::subtopic:6e01e7e7be7d9894", "source_id": "b4fedf3c3a0dd971", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing", "topic": "Introduction of Investing", "subtopic": "Asset Liquidity", "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Funds for short-term goals are generally held in an account that allows you to access the funds quickly without any tax penalties or significant fees.", "question": "In introductory investing, what does asset liquidity refer to?", "answer": "Asset liquidity refers to how quickly and easily you can access funds. For short-term goals, the source describes using an account that allows quick access without tax penalties or significant fees.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 2886, "output_tokens": 226}}
